    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct's `OwnerMapper`, so `initials` needed to exist in both places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` has an `initials` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping that computes it:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nFor `firstName=\"john\"`, `lastName=\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`, matching the acceptance test's `$.initials` assertion.",
